question: >
  On formalisation spend — whether a concept is given a full formal apparatus
  before use, or the smallest commitment that lets work proceed — the records
  assert both minimum sufficient commitment (3 judgments, 0 authored) and heavy
  specification (11 judgments, 1 authored). Which should be the stated rule, and
  where is the exception?

why_it_matters: >
  Until this is answered, a record below Dave inherits whichever side it happens
  to copy. Full draft pending: the proposal batch for this axis did not
  complete; the axis, poles, counts and evidence are real, the options below are
  the generic form.

